      "hash": "29887a5ff9846ccc23327565a07e17fa6dcaea6211f1898ae825f84ae38f4223"
    },
    {
      "id": "ddcb31afe2fbf9708bc56dcc7bb85a9982808f7461dc63195ff37e13ae8d2420",
      "text": "Next lesson",
      "hash": "d0ae2a13d8665949dd104a2fbdedcc8bca3e647a1e131d1ebaeb31c189a553b4"
    },
    {
      "id": "741dfeb3db63554db311a403ffa48fb19127a94c0eab9cee74b13321bc86420b",
      "text": "On this page",
      "hash": "b5658fc8edda24f9c94eabac9e536e0a18e3055a8ca255f9d1b8f256ea02a6cc"
    },
    {
      "id": "a1164639c161b0b93ca4f4d4f63fd5da95cc13def9b46b258c35bbd374fde943",
      "text": "The LLM Process Flow",
      "hash": "b3abace2f7fba51398d795acf056d126b31d35d0f5c814a9cde2e54d9fe14e73"
    },
    {
      "id": "5c5b3ac8937e9261b70b4839932a5ca8144858862eeafc4ef74527bea271f869",
      "text": "How Tokens Are Created",
      "hash": "81da73eda1d0da2770d8471f242df7565cad5444b1a0c3436ae9befe2c4757e2"
    },
    {
      "id": "294bb437191841faaa77c3af69fd7f553cc4ad0892906248bab1cd201ac9971b",
      "text": "Vocabulary Size Matters",
      "hash": "7e73de4aa7de0f1941751b7298841c6ce194bd7d7463516fbd3c1f734434507b"
    },
    {
      "id": "9316f6f7157d8ae3677340309ba8dc11c3a790ba7cdcd7296fa2a9edfd1b4f48",
      "text": "Handling Unusual Words",
      "hash": "811d29318abebba0aeea021e3461a56c462f70fb3d4a969c595897487e508ba6"
    },
    {
      "id": "f96c8f5e30cc8bc43f2a6c712247dfd36590a7bd1f89ac43a308e561a2630693",
      "text": "Final Thoughts",
      "hash": "68b600e35257625a075203d67c077abd17cd76aa581e447d55d5fcb061be4f5b"
    },
    {
      "id": "73b9a2695b3418258182ba5d836efa05622eac2bfcbc564f24873aaf66db83c2",
      "text": "Up next",
      "hash": "e31da5b25f8b7324861e9aadaf5c503e7fd43e739fa3be17ebe63e999fb13df1"
    },
    {
      "id": "073f5a1fb0ddccba751577c31134a7a4742bdcd34e463d72ed4042aec0524b87",
      "text": "Tokens are the fundamental building blocks that help Large Language Models (LLMs) process text. Understanding them is essential, especially since you're billed based on token usage.",
      "hash": "6af0e3f4450d31ac2cbd9252fe37c8aed34ae4bfc9ff1dec1245cb64eb51dac5"
    },
    {
      "id": "23b346154794bccee1c56430e5de424654df87ba829c9928a35c89f3473adf6e",
      "text": "Tokens are simply numbers that represent how the LLM \"thinks\" about the text you provide. The process of converting text into tokens is called",
      "hash": "fb3917ce78c30a023e271d958e9e78bdd073441c39f3aa5ffa5c5f7199b1a289"
    },
    {
      "id": "7519e0c2234439e9ef0b18f1937b0c3b11079c8e9eea23ea096a10fab1b34453",
      "text": "The tokenization process works in two parts:",
      "hash": "e954dafee3f3d0f9928eb24f0d7073cdce9c8a6257a2a5ff021d91ecba2b1a17"
    },
    {
      "id": "af8e3e359454218997871f7c29fccef6190e93aa4c8d599b56e3e73a2db7ae64",
      "text": "The tokenizer splits text into tokens it recognizes",
      "hash": "1a6378cb3d6221158b0672394b47aae08ae2773feb27f284b50675a59b30ce6a"
    },
    {
      "id": "194edf60940ca59f3cf9d630970ef066afb743c490bfcda966a49334f101af07",
      "text": "These tokens are converted into numbers",
      "hash": "eaee1e523bdbb4a6f5214c88b0e6fa6e417cbe2f903d23a6fc73f0e219f89a17"
    },
    {
      "id": "8ce81ee06f5fb222693844444e9373e1d8645b5a33137802cc18e5b607c43e8f",
      "text": "Decoding is the reverse process:",
      "hash": "dd64e876afc79952712d8e2f0457f9bb58a6373551c77a8e29ddd49a692aa0b4"
    },
    {
      "id": "bfe8327c5911166179c15ba94873442fc09e85dfcfc341366fde72e96d91c4b8",
      "text": "Numbers are converted back into text tokens",
      "hash": "97dfa1eb83727ec5a012142a902d355e84bb5f6f5c94bc389ea1eb9037b891ae"
    },
    {
      "id": "ce1fb40c98d3df80ca8e28ce384ac01c39c10b05fc89bbc227788035fb8adb58",
      "text": "The tokens are joined together to form the output",
      "hash": "eefd28b68c6b813df9585f50a4e5780340eb6015406601a5b9205525816f86aa"
    },
    {
      "id": "e5043973031355d986887db548ee34b01fbf4cb21d3da6d28245c2a90ac47c5d",
      "text": "Go deeper:",
      "hash": "15ad3d88c6733d9b257c322d3afecc9bce2b18558171007db87598c118ca17f9"
    },
    {
      "id": "942c89df2fe78c89bba9ed6a54174514f333e43be86352d6dbe1a583ff4c4ca7",
      "text": "join the waitlist for AI Coding for Real Engineers",
      "hash": "16c3492a8464a0859c944e287a9d433e9a2635f22a6bd8aad59f88c3e80ab732"
    },
    {
      "id": "befaaa67cca37942f1e2a167256f657479ade2548587031d4fbff4e9bd5fe140",
      "text": "The complete LLM process looks like this:",
      "hash": "bfbc9844f3482f1618d2d6f09d48ee614e6a7b53741ee105f952f92f4b1bcbcd"
    },
    {
      "id": "b1b36ffd3250d780acdddcce3a7efe7655127b87a81be254149c66d9d7e9dab3",
      "text": "Tokenizer encodes your input text into tokens",
      "hash": "3808a70d4fe67580b5e99bf132eb22a24492de3c60b97582be828ce0697baed9"
    },
    {
      "id": "8a51e303eb37bd489d978db904db7b162f433e82715910d76899b9c1ab08b07e",
      "text": "LLM processes your tokens",
      "hash": "55460ac1ae4e49a0b1160392b00d242bf40636fdb37a85d2eabf864385c4903b"
    },
    {
      "id": "5de9bcaa10d93ec69b394bdeb5931ad1900e890ed05a5b7a426ec5e51cc45693",
      "text": "LLM produces",
      "hash": "f53de0887c1c4b5c41c59855c4c17b0b2c4f9ad15c0f9c5a89ed9573e5b45ddf"
    },
    {
      "id": "23a32a503749e1432549f4798416b5c3a9b8302844eb266a1e7433bd45926538",
      "text": "output tokens",
      "hash": "b6798bcee84a53a994de8822f2954fb739ce9a8eb119121f36b363fe86182357"
    },
    {
      "id": "3f428d8cb722fd33af01a8e58ff68f808430f39c1991373c95c0ffaeae716ff2",
      "text": "Output tokens are decoded back into readable text",
      "hash": "1d7abf667a87131ea5896cec26b70c22ddf6f42fc5d9849456222f0b238d2f0f"
    },
    {
      "id": "11e7620ee672d265d048fcc99704fcd601c627930358467bd76ec86ed620331f",
      "text": "To clarify,",
      "hash": "021a4a3894b6f35d83d5bbd7aed869fe23a1c2132086f1ff9f5ff7f3c7d52d2e"
    },
    {
      "id": "ac9e4bcf3db785adba1256ca2a8532f6adca906c80b913fa20b1865597d887ed",
      "text": "input tokens",
      "hash": "f0c1cb4cda1985a408b12908c01227b01065a8cdfc2a03e2106ca60275f27d16"
    },
    {
      "id": "2e09d0cdf511f1c834a64547155538f0c8b994c6e8d931cfd85586a5681f76d1",
      "text": "include:",
      "hash": "e97a9b64df0d7f6f7f8afff0654bf2a55ba57ffb9b7ed288e06122b0ea5ce203"
    },
    {
      "id": "49bdcc493306a9ddfb6b3fa9667dfe7d0a51e46c04b4a6eb722ec98d7df81120",
      "text": "Your conversation history with the LLM",
      "hash": "0a121ffd97ef56497228efca25d277bb36ae901872a6fa26c61307de5f82f41c"
    },
    {
      "id": "0dfa83b7ac1954f5064b935c468f160bcee405fd7028644040c094165b1da520",
      "text": "System prompts",
      "hash": "3a5be058243d495fa1b1699f22599a16af68d85e4684f88ab5fb6657b150556e"
    },
    {
      "id": "da4aad9763512d450f45882d0a969a09e1007299c302ee61de255504e38602f0",
      "text": "Tool definitions",
      "hash": "4c78eb66d53b16f7fea3bac69ced9fb54c0756be848bebb64125305f95538d20"
    },
    {
      "id": "eb642023257afec5d7be3921581af141dc749ff905d189cdd5bfd64a29316055",
      "text": "Output tokens are what the LLM sends back as a response.",
      "hash": "3abc654af74bc201b8eafe12936f949ac34d3e977becd85f1b03e250f25dd21a"
    },
    {
      "id": "09899714227af964a131f5e6e9e991f81680e4b6a1f636fa83896eec166871d6",
      "text": "You're billed for both input and output tokens, typically at different rates. One way to save money is to design your prompts to generate fewer output tokens.",
      "hash": "013e137909c502668b20c0e63c7e277454094f9db7be0372184ff8aad56e7f27"
    },
    {
      "id": "c81dfa261dbfefd38a5488008fd0e3707d523a1ecabed4aa013653c8583cfb94",
      "text": "The tokenization process starts with a large corpus of text - similar to what's used to train the LLM itself. Let's imagine a tiny corpus consisting of just one sentence: \"the cat sat on the mat.\"",
      "hash": "7e9f23f78d87ffa8ac62eba63bd7693cc6c7a46cfdf242e2e154c1af6078b15d"
    },
    {
      "id": "7b2671b638ed9db421436651e11b8adc7558e8f1ceeb98047225d8c951adda2b",
      "text": "First, all individual characters are extracted:",
      "hash": "9a67937640ecee89e1400bccf59add54472cca4fc9f70e102dabe49d625d4efa"
    },
    {
      "id": "77446d7c77784fb97134399f6144614c0db3516751cfc3a8ee0209ac337bce43",
      "text": "Each of these characters becomes its own token in the vocabulary.",
      "hash": "16710a25fa5e05a65a9a9756e2888f134e897ea289f6db57a2352b12393342c3"
    },
    {
      "id": "28077dff94a47a364d4142753f519bcb6257e5ef74a3bc84691ed54f6aaee45b",
      "text": "Next, common groupings of characters are identified:",
      "hash": "0e3b0f5f766076b55f19896cd5e76df1d8d441d68bf9029dd471db7b2075ef29"
    },
    {
      "id": "6125d14cb13539d7cf7c6484d50fc32c20a9283adee78a6af4b309e372e43b95",
      "text": "\"TH\" appears in \"the\" (twice)",
      "hash": "ec1f26cf9c5c8cb6580192a4ecc772f499f4d8150cf468da75734a466fe7d321"
    },
    {
      "id": "7671ecf3e4e72de6d69ab7d1662c9a5afe9bd76573cf06ab3980c3ecfd00ddf9",
      "text": "\"HE\" appears in \"the\" (twice)",
      "hash": "6b66eac3334ae6994bd43324fff6315c52f13a5a481cbbcea28edd0c29426888"
    },
    {
      "id": "9129913435379df79b0b8e94cc1efb2a9e6b93ba04d5e211fea0e49af1780553",
      "text": "\"AT\" appears in \"cat\", \"sat\", and \"mat\"",
      "hash": "4833d69a741855bd7a7421e0764694e3d9530df3a3e882548c6e00bc2ccd9aa7"
    },
    {
      "id": "0675063163cdffd6c0952cab53468e4167151a507400715923a1040677396a6d",
      "text": "Each of these groupings also gets assigned its own token.",
      "hash": "5f6ef0ade7a093ea0f29be917d7d551c94bbb9a9efbebe599ccc488ed14ca7dc"
    },
    {
      "id": "a472fd8505518daa239bfba4dca14fdaf72f224a644f4ec1203bf0aa5efc5cb8",
      "text": "Then, groups of groups are identified - like \"TH\" + \"HE\" creating \"THE\" (the word \"the\"), which gets its own token.",
      "hash": "dc14f39f560ffad3a77b389052e789dbbbd850b8cfa613674b3c66b9efcfac98"
    },
    {
      "id": "8969d0fd6559305dc455e854e52c26e12412968989258c978b8a5387d52162ad",
      "text": "The goal is to create a large vocabulary of tokens because larger vocabularies can split words into fewer tokens, making processing more efficient.",
      "hash": "a36d9cf5c22ea46cb6cbf1b94e21f73a22027a4503a2cf90dc764edfb39d7251"
    },
    {
      "id": "fc1a194620b31a3a7169a6a6d841592c6ac7b590bf2bea4d268227fbdc8f5150",
      "text": "For example, a vocabulary size of 1,000 tokens might split \"understanding\" into 5 tokens. A vocabulary size of 50,000 tokens might split it into 3 tokens, and a vocabulary size of 200,000 tokens might split it into 2 tokens.",
      "hash": "e71249da508055c86c4c3d53ce86eb0b894551f7c5fdc7c8503fe9af68ddbf0f"
    },
    {
      "id": "d9937d8d5a528bfacdd616a6d49e79c3da61e7d350b263b2089a8e787dd862ae",
      "text": "Having a larger vocabulary means you can split words into fewer tokens, making processing more efficient.",
      "hash": "d56ee286b0ae5bc8e833712b820cb465a96452c2b7330e385cc1a535fca8daf2"
    },
    {
      "id": "4e2a0db892a86e9a558b2ed5f61fbd86a99dbd5506f68fa382c1d6eab9cbdbe2",
      "text": "The tokenizer struggles with uncommon words. For example, \"O Frabjous Day\" from Lewis Carroll's poem gets split into many tokens because \"Frabjous\" is a made-up word that doesn't appear frequently in the training corpus.",
      "hash": "e57555aeaeba7a8af7665219ce87df78d9b1820a16c2a8d143013fea10740264"
    },
    {
      "id": "11ae16c68644f9daa74ac1d6ebbdd279f31205b6ca2035d54e935e8c2e7afdc6",
      "text": "We can see that it turns it into 7 tokens - more than we'd expect from only 15 characters.",
      "hash": "551b6681c464a72491c72c273d98c44ec6f5df21681e6a4b9ad90401244ff7c6"
    },
    {
      "id": "7bd850640503464d6c9eeddd1fbaec7b95c700caa6c9592d9c5cacdc70b68b9a",
      "text": "I hope that helps demystify tokens a bit. I found the",
      "hash": "dc39810fc2c580a63e86a86d2032da3c47702ec7b91db4ed91e9e80be2ad6731"
    },
    {
      "id": "f5e052a77ea92949f7fd540718a7f4e08bcdfd5b73f8de0449ceb056124f9c21",
      "text": "tiktokenizer playground",
      "hash": "b5ee71d176844595289dde181c5fcda141e38bd0d84560705e608bb4d8aa4a87"
    },
    {
      "id": "d36559400e57ac9ca12519080169b1db32567e328f5e9c89bd9bc7abf59f04ee",
      "text": "really useful for understanding this stuff.",
      "hash": "ace9253a7cd1de6d38b1359aa6d51c4baf6e72cf5115d497ce90ac8a6293a277"
    },
    {
      "id": "09fb49a8710538765de282ce9b4f29c6667547bdc0797a7a8dfe18212f65f519",
      "text": "Let me know if you have any questions - and what else would you like me to cover next?",
